+"What does the evolution towards agentic AI bring us, according to the lecture?","['EVOLUTION TOWARD AGENTIC AI Era Agent Type Key Feature Example 1990s Reactive Respond to stimuli Subsumption robot 2000s Deliberative Plan before actingBDI model (Poole & Mackworth Ch. 4) 2010s Cognitive Learn & reason IBM Watson 2020s Agentic AIUse LLMs to understand, plan & actChatGPT Agents, AutoGPT 22', 'AGENTIC AI •Agentic AI refers to AI systems that can act independently , make decisions, and perform tasks to achieve specific goals. •These systems combine reasoning, memory, and generative abilities to plan and adapt their actions. •Unlike traditional AI, they don’t just respond — they take initiative and collaborate with humans or other agents. 26', 'INTENTIONAL STANCE IN TODAY’S AI •LLMs and agentic AI often seem to make choices or have goals •When we say “ChatGPT understands” or “the agent decides,” we’re using the intentional stance •These systems don’t truly think, but this view helps us explain and predict their behaviour •Talking about AI “as if it thinks” makes human –AI interaction easier to understand. 37', 'SUMMARY •Recognised key trends in computing •Defined agents, multi -agent systems, and Agentic AI •Discussed how multi -agent systems enable agents to work together on complex tasks •Agentic AI is the next step: a systems that understand, reason, create, and collaborate with humans 38', 'SUMMARY •This lecture has looked in detail at what constitutes an intelligent agent •We looked at the properties of an intelligent agent and the properties of the environments in which it may operate •We introduced the intentional stance and discussed its use •Finally, we discussed what kinds of task an agent might need to carry out. 50']","According to the context, the evolution towards agentic AI brings us systems that:
