+What is the primary goal of modern AI according to the lecture?,"['[Course Metadata] Course: BAXI 3113 INTELLIGENT AGENT; Lecturer/Author: Dr. Nur Zareen Zulkarnain; Department: Intelligent Computing and Analytics (ICA)\n\n---\n\nFROM AUTOMATION TO COLLABORATION • Traditional AI = Task automation • Follows fixed rules and performs predefined tasks • Efficient but limited by human instructions • Modern AI = Goal-driven collaboration • Understands goals and adapts to user needs • Uses reasoning and creativity to co-create solutions • Collaboration replaces command-and-control • AI acts as a partner, not just a tool 18', '[Course Metadata] Course: BAXI 3113 INTELLIGENT AGENT; Lecturer/Author: Dr. Nur Zareen Zulkarnain; Department: Intelligent Computing and Analytics (ICA)\n\n---\n\nJOINT INTENTIONS • The termination condition is achieved when an agent realizes that the goal is satisfied, impossible, the motivation is no longer present and so on. • But it doesn’t drop the goal right away • Instead, it adopts a new goal — to make this new knowledge mutually believed → this ensures that the agents are coordinated • They don’t stop working towards the goal until they are all appraised of the situation • Mutual belief is achieved by communication 12', '[Course Metadata] Course: BAXI 3113 INTELLIGENT AGENT; Lecturer/Author: Dr. Nur Zareen Zulkarnain; Department: Intelligent Computing and Analytics (ICA)\n\n---\n\nAGENTS: A FIRST DEFINITION • An agent is a computer system that is capable of independent (autonomous) action on behalf of its user or owner • I.e., figuring out what needs to be done to satisfy design objectives, rather than constantly being told • Modern agents may use generative AI models to reason, adapt to context, and create solutions without explicit re-programming 24', '[Course Metadata] Course: BAXI 3113 INTELLIGENT AGENT; Lecturer/Author: Dr. Nur Zareen Zulkarnain; Department: Intelligent Computing and Analytics (ICA)\n\n---\n\nUSE TOO MUCH AI • Temptation to focus on intelligent aspects of the application • An agent framework too overburdened with experimental AI techniques to be usable • Resist temptation to believe such features are essential in your system • build agents with a minimum of AI • success is obtained with such systems, progressively evolve them into richer systems 11 Macro (Society) LevelPolitical Management Conceptual Analysis & Design Micro (Agent) Level', '[Course Metadata] Course: BAXI 3113 INTELLIGENT AGENT; Lecturer/Author: Dr. Nur Zareen Zulkarnain; Department: Intelligent Computing and Analytics (ICA)\n\n---\n\nJOINT INTENTIONS • Just as we have individual intentions, we can have joint intentions for a team of agents • Levesque defined the idea of a joint persistent goal (JPG). • A group of agents have a collective commitment to bring about some goal φ, “move the couch” • Agents don’t believe that φ is satisfied, but believe it is possible. • Agents maintain the goal φ until a termination condition is reached. 11']","According to the context, the primary goal of modern AI is ""Goal-driven collaboration"". This is stated in [S1] (source: 1.pdf, page: 18) as a replacement for traditional AI, which follows fixed rules and performs predefined tasks.",Modern AI = Goal-driven collaboration,0.6666666666666666,0.896170957983677,0.8666666666377778,1.0
