+What was the main focus of the reactive agents in the 1990s era?,"['[Course Metadata] Course: BAXI 3113 INTELLIGENT AGENT; Lecturer/Author: Dr. Nur Zareen Zulkarnain; Department: Intelligent Computing and Analytics (ICA)\n\n---\n\nEVOLUTION TOWARD AGENTIC AI Era Agent Type Key Feature Example 1990s Reactive Respond to stimuli Subsumption robot 2000s Deliberative Plan before acting BDI model (Poole & Mackworth Ch. 4) 2010s Cognitive Learn & reason IBM Watson 2020s Agentic AI Use LLMs to understand, plan & act ChatGPT Agents, AutoGPT 22', '[Course Metadata] Course: BAXI 3113 INTELLIGENT AGENT; Lecturer/Author: Dr. Nur Zareen Zulkarnain; Department: Intelligent Computing and Analytics (ICA)\n\n---\n\nAGENT-BASED ANALYSIS • Analysis aims to understand, at least • What are the main actors interacting with the system • How the system interacts with these actors • What the system is supposed to do • Then, we associate accordingly • Roles responsibilities and capabilities • Interaction patterns between agents 5', '[Course Metadata] Course: BAXI 3113 INTELLIGENT AGENT; Lecturer/Author: Dr. Nur Zareen Zulkarnain; Department: Intelligent Computing and Analytics (ICA)\n\n---\n\nSOME VIEWS OF THE FIELD • We want to build systems of interacting, autonomous agents, but we don’t yet know what these systems should look like • You can take a “neat” or “scruffy” approach to the problem, seeing it as a problem of theory or a problem of engineering 37 Primarily a search for appropriate theoretical foundations', '[Course Metadata] Course: BAXI 3113 INTELLIGENT AGENT; Lecturer/Author: Dr. Nur Zareen Zulkarnain; Department: Intelligent Computing and Analytics (ICA)\n\n---\n\nLEARNING OUTCOMES At the end of today’s lecture, you should be able to: • Identify trends in the history of computing • Explain agents and multiagent system • Determine appropriate implementation of agents in various fields 5', '[Course Metadata] Course: BAXI 3113 INTELLIGENT AGENT; Lecturer/Author: Dr. Nur Zareen Zul