+"What does the evolution towards agentic AI bring us, according to the lecture?","['[Course Metadata] Course: BAXI 3113 INTELLIGENT AGENT; Lecturer/Author: Dr. Nur Zareen Zulkarnain; Department: Intelligent Computing and Analytics (ICA)\n\n---\n\nEVOLUTION TOWARD AGENTIC AI Era Agent Type Key Feature Example 1990s Reactive Respond to stimuli Subsumption robot 2000s Deliberative Plan before acting BDI model (Poole & Mackworth Ch. 4) 2010s Cognitive Learn & reason IBM Watson 2020s Agentic AI Use LLMs to understand, plan & act ChatGPT Agents, AutoGPT 22', '[Course Metadata] Course: BAXI 3113 INTELLIGENT AGENT; Lecturer/Author: Dr. Nur Zareen Zulkarnain; Department: Intelligent Computing and Analytics (ICA)\n\n---\n\nAGENTIC AI • Agentic AI refers to AI systems that can act independently, make decisions, and perform tasks to achieve specific goals. • These systems combine reasoning, memory, and generative abilities to plan and adapt their actions. • Unlike traditional AI, they don’t just respond — they take initiative and collaborate with humans or other agents. 26', '[Course Metadata] Course: BAXI 3113 INTELLIGENT AGENT; Lecturer/Author: Dr. Nur Zareen Zulkarnain; Department: Intelligent Computing and Analytics (ICA)\n\n---\n\nSUMMARY • Recognised key trends in computing • Defined agents, multi-agent systems, and Agentic AI • Discussed how multi-agent systems enable agents to work together on complex tasks • Agentic AI is the next step: a systems that understand, reason, create, and collaborate with humans 38', '[Course Metadata] Course: BAXI 3113 INTELLIGENT AGENT; Lecturer/Author: Dr. Nur Zareen Zulkarnain; Department: Intelligent Computing and Analytics (ICA)\n\n---\n\nWHERE DOES THIS BRINGS US? • Delegation and Intelligence imply the need to build computer systems that can act effectively on our behalf • This implies: • The ability of computer systems to act independently • The ability of computer systems to act in a way that represents our best interests while interacting with other humans or systems 20', '[Course Metadata] Course: BAXI 3113 INTELLIGENT AGENT; Lecturer/Author: Dr. Nur Zareen Zulkarnain; Department: Intelligent Computing and Analytics (ICA)\n\n---\n\nSUMMARY • Overall, of the three lectures: • Key assumption: benevolence • Agents are working together, not in competition • In today’s lecture, We discussed a number of ways of having agents decide what to do, and make sure that their work is coordinated 14']","According to the lecture, the evolution towards agentic AI brings us the need to build computer systems that can act effectively on our behalf, specifically:
