s by discussing the needs, issues and typology associated to it • Differentiate Telescript and TCL/TK 2', '[Course Metadata] Course: BAXI 3113 INTELLIGENT AGENT; Lecturer/Author: Dr. Nur Zareen Zulkarnain; Department: Intelligent Computing and Analytics (ICA)\n\n---\n\nAGENTS: A FIRST DEFINITION • An agent is a computer system that is capable of independent (autonomous) action on behalf of its user or owner • I.e., figuring out what needs to be done to satisfy design objectives, rather than constantly being told • Modern agents may use generative AI models to reason, adapt to context, and create solutions without explicit re-programming 24']","The key idea of agent-oriented programming as introduced by Yoav Shoham is not explicitly mentioned in the provided context. However, based on the information provided, it can be inferred that the key idea is to move away from machine-oriented views of programming and towards concepts and metaphors that more closely reflect the way humans understand the world.
