+What is the primary goal of modern AI according to the lecture?,"['FROM AUTOMATION TO COLLABORATION • Traditional AI = Task automation • Follows fixed rules and performs predefined tasks • Efficient but limited by human instructions • Modern AI = Goal-driven collaboration • Understands goals and adapts to user needs • Uses reasoning and creativity to co-create solutions • Collaboration replaces command-and-control • AI acts as a partner, not just a tool 18', 'SYMBOLIC AI - CRITICS • Recall symbolic AI in Deductive Reasoning Agent lecture. • Is inference on symbols representing the world sufficient to solve real-world problems? • Problems with “symbolic AI”: • Computational complexity of reasoning in real-world applications • The transduction/knowledge acquisition bottleneck • Logic-based approaches largely focus on theoretical reasoning • Detached from interaction with physical world 3', 'LEARNING OUTCOMES At the end of today’s lecture, you should be able to: • Recognise agent behaviours • Compare agent with objects and AI systems • Justify agents as intentional system • Identify tasks for agents 2', 'AGENTIC AI • Agentic AI refers to AI systems that can act independently, make decisions, and perform tasks to achieve specific goals. • These systems combine reasoning, memory, and generative abilities to plan and adapt their actions. • Unlike traditional AI, they don’t just respond — they take initiative and collaborate with humans or other agents. 26', 'INTENTIONAL STANCE IN TODAY’S AI • LLMs and agentic AI often seem to make choices or have goals • When we say “ChatGPT understands” or “the agent decides,” we’re using the intentional stance • These systems don’t truly think, but this view helps us explain and predict their behaviour • Talking about AI “as if it thinks” makes human–AI interaction easier to understand. 37']","According to the lecture, the primary goal of modern AI is to enable collaboration. Specifically, the lecture states that modern AI aims to ""understand goals and adapt to user needs,"" and it uses reasoning and creativity to co-create solutions. Modern AI is designed to work collaboratively with humans, not just as tools, and it acts as a partner, not just an automated process.",Modern AI = Goal-driven collaboration,1.0,0.99233122928498,0.7499999999625,1.0
+What are the three key features of an agent according to the lecture?,"['SUMMARY • Overall, of the three lectures: • Key assumption: benevolence • Agents are working together, not in competition • In today’s lecture, We discussed a number of ways of having agents decide what to do, and make sure that their work is coordinated 14', 'SUMMARY • In this lecture, we looked at a few key pitfalls of agent development • We categorized it to 6 categories: • Political • Management • Conceptual • Analysis & Design • Micro (Agent) • Macro (Society) Level 16', 'WHAT IS AN AGENT? • The main point about agents is they are autonomous: capable independent action 4 An agent is a computer system that is situated in some environment, and that is capable of autonomous action in that environment in order to meet its delegated objectives • It is all about decisions: • An agent must choose what action to perform • An agent must decide when to perform an action', 'SUMMARY • This lecture has looked in detail at what constitutes an intelligent agent • We looked at the properties of an intelligent agent and the properties of the environments in which it may operate • We introduced the intentional stance and discussed its use • Finally, we discussed what kinds of task an agent might need to carry out. 50', 'AGENT ARCHITECTURES Three broad categories: 4 Deliberative Architectures focus on planning and symbolic reasoning Reactive Architectures focus on reactivity based on behavioural rules Hybrid Architectures attempt to balance proactiveness with reactivity']","Based on the lecture in S3 (L2.0 - Intelligent Agents (1).pdf, page 4), the three key features of an agent are:
