+"What does the evolution towards agentic AI bring us, according to the lecture?","['EVOLUTION TOWARD AGENTIC AI Era Agent Type Key Feature Example 1990s Reactive Respond to stimuli Subsumption robot 2000s Deliberative Plan before acting BDI model (Poole & Mackworth Ch. 4) 2010s Cognitive Learn & reason IBM Watson 2020s Agentic AI Use LLMs to understand, plan & act ChatGPT Agents, AutoGPT 22', 'AGENTIC AI • Agentic AI refers to AI systems that can act independently, make decisions, and perform tasks to achieve specific goals. • These systems combine reasoning, memory, and generative abilities to plan and adapt their actions. • Unlike traditional AI, they don’t just respond — they take initiative and collaborate with humans or other agents. 26', 'INTENTIONAL STANCE IN TODAY’S AI • LLMs and agentic AI often seem to make choices or have goals • When we say “ChatGPT understands” or “the agent decides,” we’re using the intentional stance • These systems don’t truly think, but this view helps us explain and predict their behaviour • Talking about AI “as if it thinks” makes human–AI interaction easier to understand. 37', 'SYMBOLIC AI - CRITICS • Recall symbolic AI in Deductive Reasoning Agent lecture. • Is inference on symbols representing the world sufficient to solve real-world problems? • Problems with “symbolic AI”: • Computational complexity of reasoning in real-world applications • The transduction/knowledge acquisition bottleneck • Logic-based approaches largely focus on theoretical reasoning • Detached from interaction with physical world 3', 'architectures attempt to combine the best of reasoning and reactive architectures 2012–present: Agentic AI • Agents that combine reasoning with LLMs to plan, act, and collaborate autonomously']","The evolution towards **Agentic AI** brings us a fundamental shift in how we conceptualize and interact with artificial intelligence, moving from reactive to proactive and collaborative systems.
+
+According to the lecture:
+
+1. **From Reactive to Proactive**: Traditional AI (reactive) systems respond to immediate stimuli. Agentic AI takes initiative, plans, and acts to achieve complex goals autonomously, even when no immediate trigger is present.
+
+2. **Reasoning and Memory Integration**: Agentic AI combines reasoning and memory with generative abilities, allowing it to adapt its actions and decisions over time based on context and learned patterns.
+
+3. **Collaboration with Humans**: Unlike some reactive systems, Agentic AI doesn't just respond to stimuli—it collaborates with humans or other AI agents to achieve broader, more complex objectives.
+
+4. **Out-of-Scope for Physical World**: As mentioned in the context, symbolic AI is detached from interaction with the physical world, while symbolic reasoning in deductive AI struggles with real-world complexity.
+
+5. **Human-Centric AI**: The intentional stance perspective helps explain that AI systems ""as if they think"" make choices, facilitating better understanding of human-AI interaction.
+
+In essence, Agentic AI represents a shift towards AI systems that are **intelligent, adaptive, and collaborative** rather than merely responsive, making them better suited for tasks requiring strategic planning, complex problem-solving, and human interaction.","The ability of computer systems to act independently, the ability of computer systems to act in a way that represents our best interests while interacting with other humans or systems",0.9333333333333333,0.8091659796414565,0.49999999995,0.5
