+"According to the lecture, what is the underlying problem with knowledge representation and reasoning?","['THE REPRESENTATION / REASONING PROBLEM • The underlying problem with knowledge representation / reasoning lies with the complexity of symbol manipulation algorithms. • In general many (most) search-based symbol manipulation algorithms of interest are highly intractable. • Hard to find compact representations. • Because of these problems, some researchers have looked to alternative techniques for building agents; we look at these later. 11', 'TWO ISSUES 10 The Transduction Problem The transduction problem is that of translating the real world into an accurate, adequate symbolic description, in time for that description to be useful. This has led onto research into vision, speech understanding, learning… The Representation / Reasoning Problem How to symbolically represent information about complex real-world entities and processes, and how to get agents to reason with this information in time for the results to be useful.', 'SYMBOLIC AI - CRITICS • Recall symbolic AI in Deductive Reasoning Agent lecture. • Is inference on symbols representing the world sufficient to solve real-world problems? • Problems with “symbolic AI”: • Computational complexity of reasoning in real-world applications • The transduction/knowledge acquisition bottleneck • Logic-based approaches largely focus on theoretical reasoning • Detached from interaction with physical world 3', 'LEARNING OUTCOMES At the end of this lecture, you should be able to: • Explain how means-ends reasoning fit into the basic agent control loop • Representation • Relate blocksworld to the planning problem • Practical reasoning agent implementation • Deliberation 2', 'LEARNING OUTCOMES At the end of this lecture, you should be able to: • Describe practical reasoning • Relate practical reasoning with intentions 2']","According to the lecture, the underlying problem with knowledge representation and reasoning lies with the **complexity of symbol manipulation algorithms**.
+
+Here is a breakdown of the specific issues mentioned in the source text, which aligns with this statement:
+*   **Highly Intractable:** Most search-based symbol manipulation algorithms are highly difficult to solve.
+*   **Hard to Find Compact Representations:** Finding efficient ways to encode information is difficult.
+*   **Impact of Complexity:** These difficulties make it hard to build agents, as noted by the researchers looking into alternative techniques.",The underlying problem with knowledge representation / reasoning lies with the complexity of symbol manipulation algorithms.,1.0,0.9944811307415135,0.9999999999666667,1.0
+What is the key idea of agent-oriented programming as introduced by Yoav Shoham?,"['AGENT-ORIENTED PROGRAMMING • Yoav Shoham introduced “agent-oriented programming” in 1990: “... new programming paradigm, based on a societal view of computation ...” • The key idea: • Directly programming agents in terms of intentional notions • like belief, desire, and intention • Adopts the same abstraction as humans • Resulted in the Agent0 programming language 21', 'SUMMARY • Defined the main agent architectures and symbolic reasoning approach • Discussed how logic enables deductive reasoning in agents • Introduced agent-oriented programming (Agent0, PLACA, Concurrent METATEM) • Connected classical reasoning agents to modern Agentic AI systems 35', 'SUMMARY • In this lecture, we explored why traditional object-oriented methodologies are not sufficient for building multi-agent systems. • We introduced agent-oriented methodologies that focus on roles, interactions, and coordination between agents. • We discussed examples such as GAIA, Agent UML, and Prometheus to illustrate different approaches to agent-based analysis and design. • We highlighted the importance of separating agent analysis from agent design to manage system complexity. 23', 'AGENT ORIENTED METHODOLOGIES • Each methodology may introduce further abstractions - around which to model software and to organize the software process • For example: roles, organizations, responsibilities, belief, desire and intentions • Not directly translating into concrete entities of the software system → the concept of role is an aspect of an agent, not an agent 4', 'AGENTS AS INTENTIONAL SYSTEMS 3. Post-Declarative Systems • In procedural programming, we say exactly what a system should do; • In declarative programming, we state something that we want to achieve, give the system general info about the relationships between objects, and let a built-in control mechanism (e. g. , goal-directed theorem proving) figure out what to do;']","The key idea of agent-oriented programming, introduced by Yoav Shoham, is to directly program agents using **intentional notions** (such as belief, desire, and intention) within an **abstraction** similar to humans.
+
+This approach resulted in the development of the **Agent0 programming language**.","The key idea of agent-oriented programming as introduced by Yoav Shoham is to directly program agents in terms of intentional notions like belief, desire, and intention, and to adopt the same abstraction as humans.",1.0,0.9821098168661372,0.9999999999,1.0
