+What was the main focus of the reactive agents in the 1990s era?,"['EVOLUTION TOWARD AGENTIC AI Era Agent Type Key Feature Example 1990s Reactive Respond to stimuli Subsumption robot 2000s Deliberative Plan before acting BDI model (Poole & Mackworth Ch. 4) 2010s Cognitive Learn & reason IBM Watson 2020s Agentic AI Use LLMs to understand, plan & act ChatGPT Agents, AutoGPT 22', 'CLASSES OF ARCHITECTURE 7 1956 - present: Symbolic Reasoning Agents 1985–present: Reactive Agents 1990-present: Hybrid Agents • Decides by manipulating symbols that represent knowledge • Use explicit logical reasoning to decide actions • Problems with symbolic reasoning led to a reaction against this • Hybrid architectures attempt to combine the best of reasoning and reactive architectures 2012–present:', 'AGENT ARCHITECTURES Three broad categories: 4 Deliberative Architectures focus on planning and symbolic reasoning Reactive Architectures focus on reactivity based on behavioural rules Hybrid Architectures attempt to balance proactiveness with reactivity', 'PURELY REACTIVE AGENTS • Some agents decide what to do without reference to their history they base their decision making entirely on the present, with no reference at all to the past • We call such agents purely reactive: • A thermostat is a purely reactive agent. 39', 'architectures attempt to combine the best of reasoning and reactive architectures 2012–present: Agentic AI • Agents that combine reasoning with LLMs to plan, act, and collaborate autonomously']","The main focus of reactive agents in the 1990s era was **responding to stimuli and executing simple, task-oriented actions**.
