+"What is the side effect or package deal problem, and how does it relate to practical reasoning?","The side effect or package deal problem in practical reasoning is that agents do not necessarily intend all the expected side effects of their intentions. For instance, believing that going to the dentist involves pain does not imply that one intends to suffer pain.
+
+### Relations to Practical Reasoning
+- Practical reasoning involves understanding and planning actions with their potential outcomes.
+- The problem highlights that intentions may not encompass all expected consequences, complicating the planning process.
+- It challenges the simple assumption that all outcomes of an intended action are directly intended.
+
