+- **Closed World Assumption**: The ontology follows the closed world assumption, which implies that the absence of information about a particular situation is taken to mean that such a situation does not occur. In other words, if something is not explicitly mentioned, it is considered false.
+- **Components of the Environment**: The blocksworld includes a robot arm, three blocks (A, B, and C) of equal size, and a tabletop. These components are the core elements that the planning problem targets, which involves arranging the blocks on the table-top.
