+What are the two approaches to automated argumentation discussed in the text?,"The two approaches to automated argumentation discussed are abstract argumentation and deductive argumentation.
+
+### Explanation
+- **Abstract Argumentation** (S1, S3):
+  - Abstract argumentation examines how arguments co-exist. [S1]
+  - It involves looking at how different arguments can coexist, resolving conflicts between them. [S3]
+  - In abstract argumentation, attacks between arguments can be identified, leading to the determination of preferred extensions or grounded extensions. [S3]
+
+- **Deductive Argumentation** (S1, S4, S5):
+  - Deductive argumentation models arguments using logical formulae. [S4]
+  - It involves reasoning that can be rebutted, where premises and warrants can be challenged. [S5]
+  - In deductive argumentation, conclusions can be rebutted, allowing for the identification of attacks and subsequent analysis of preferred extensions or grounded extensions. [S3]
