+What is the purpose of the subscribe/notify pattern in OO systems?,"The purpose of the subscribe/notify pattern in Object-Oriented (OO) systems is to facilitate information proactively shared between objects, enabling one object to register interest in certain events and receiving notifications when those events occur.
+
+- As described in [S2] and [S1], objects in subscribe/notify pattern can subscribe to another object indicating they are interested in certain events. When an event occurs, the subscribed object is notified.
+- This pattern aims to reduce the necessity of objects needing to know about the interests of other objects, thus simplifying the relationships between objects and enhancing modularity.
+
+Sources: [S1], [S2]","['RESULT SHARING IN SUBSCRIBE/NOTIFY PATTERN •Common design pattern in OO systems: subscribe/notify •An object subscribes to another object, saying “tell me when event e happens” •When event e happens, original object is notified •Information pro -actively shared between objects •Objects required to know about the interests of other objects → inform objects when relevant information arises 9'
