+What is the expected value of an action by an agent in a blackboard control mechanism difficult to determine?,"In a blackboard control mechanism, the expected value of an action by an agent is difficult to determine due to complex interrelationships among the agents, as mentioned in [S1].
+
+- **Complex Interrelationships Among Agents**: The interconnections between different agents can lead to unpredictable outcomes and make it hard to predict the value of an action. Agents may have different goals, knowledge, and capabilities, which can influence the expected value.
+- **Difficulty in Determining Expected Value**: The control mechanism must account for both goal-directed and data-directed factors. Determining the expected value of an action involves considering not only the goals of the agent but also the data available, which may involve integrating diverse sources of information and understanding their interdependencies. This integration can be complex and challenging to manage effectively, especially in a dynamic and interconnected environment.
+
