+What are the three types of mobile agents mentioned in the document?,"The three types of mobile agents mentioned in the document are: Autonomous, On-demand, and 'Active mail'.
+
+- Autonomous mobile agents are those that operate independently without direct control from a host or another agent. They are designed to handle tasks on their own, moving from one location to another as needed.
+- On-demand mobile agents are triggered by certain conditions or requests, similar to how software might be activated by user input or system events. They are useful for executing tasks that require specific actions at designated times.
+- 'Active mail' refers to a type of mobile agent that is specifically designed for tasks involving emails or communication over a network. These agents are capable of moving between different locations to deliver or manage emails efficiently.
+
+Sources: [S1], [S3]","['MOBILE AGENT TYPOLOGY 11 We can divide mobile agents into at least three types Autonomous On-demand ‘Active mail’'
+ 'LEARNING OUTCOMES At the end of this lecture, you should be able to: •Understand the need of agent -oriented methodologies •State different types of agent -oriented methodologies •Explain mobile agents by discussing the needs, issues and typology associated to it •Differentiate Telescript and TCL/TK 2'
+ 'MOBILE AGENTS Why mobile agents? •low-bandwidth networks •efficient use of network resources There are many issues when building software tools that can support mobile agents: •security for hosts and agents •heterogeneity of hosts •dynamic linking 10'
+ 'AGENTS IN TELESCRIPT •Agents are mobile : they are able to move from one place to another using a ticket , which specifies the parameters of its journey: •destination •completion time •Agents can communicate with one -another: •if they occupy different places, then they can connect across a network •if they occupy the same location, then they can meet one another 17'
+ 'RESOURCES •TELESCRIPT agents have an associated permit , which specifies: •what the agent can do (e.g., limitations on travel) •what resources the agent can use •The most important resources are: •‘money’, measured in ‘ teleclicks ’ (which correspond to real money) •lifetime (measured in seconds) •size (measured in bytes) •Agents and places are executed by an engine which is a kind of agent operating system 18']","We can divide mobile agents into at least three types: Autonomous, On-demand, and Active mail",1.0,0.9343246483646408,0.99999999998,1.0
