+ '18Agents are autonomous : •agents embody stronger notion of autonomy than objects, and in particular, they decide for themselves whether or not to perform an action on request from another agent Agents are smart : •capable of flexible (reactive, pro -active, social) behaviour – the standard object -oriented model has nothing to say about such types of behaviour Agents are active : •not passive service providers; a multi -agent system is inherently multi -threaded, in that each agent is assumed']",The main point about agents is they are autonomous : capable independent action,1.0,0.9999999999998996,0.99999999998,1.0
