+What does a reactive system maintain an ongoing interaction with its environment to do?,"A reactive system maintains an ongoing interaction with its environment to respond to changes that occur in it, ensuring timely responses that are useful for the current situation.
+
+- The definition from [S1] (page 9) explicitly states that a reactive system is one that interacts with its environment continuously and responds to changes. This interaction and response are crucial for maintaining relevance and utility in dynamic environments.
+- Further elaboration in [S1] (page 9) highlights the necessity of a reactive system to handle potential failures dynamically, ensuring it can adapt to changing conditions effectively.
+
+Sources: [S1], [S3]","['REACTIVITY •Software is hard to build for dynamic domains: program must consider possibility of failure •A reactive system is one that maintains an ongoing interaction with its environment and responds to changes that occur in it (in time for the response to be useful). 9'
