+What is the main difference between Blind commitment and Single-minded commitment?,"Blind commitment and single-minded commitment both deal with maintaining an intention until it is achieved or deemed impossible, but blind commitment is more reactive, overcommitted to intentions, and never considers the appropriateness of its intentions, while single-minded commitment stops to determine whether intentions have succeeded or if they are impossible.
+
+- **Blind Commitment**: Makes the control loop more reactive, able to change intention when the world changes. However, it is still overcommitted to intentions and never stops to consider whether or not its intentions are appropriate.
+- **Single-minded Commitment**: Stops to determine whether intentions have succeeded or if they are impossible. This allows the agent to reconsider its intentions after executing a plan, achieving current intentions, or believing intentions are no longer possible.
+
+**Sources: [S1], [S4]**","['DEGREES OF COMMITMENT Blind commitment •A blindly committed agent will continue to maintain an intention until it believes the intention has actually been achieved . Blind commitment is also sometimes referred to as fanatical commitment. Single -minded commitment •A single -minded agent will continue to maintain an intention until it believes that either the intention has been achieved , or else that it is no longer possible to achieve the intention. 3'
