+What is the Monotonic Concession Protocol?,"The Monotonic Concession Protocol is a negotiation strategy described in the lecture notes. It involves rounds where agents propose deals and an agreement is reached if a proposal is at least as good as the other's proposal. If no agreement is reached, the process repeats. In subsequent rounds, agents cannot propose a deal that the other prefers less, leading to a guaranteed finite negotiation process.
+
+Sources: [S2], [S3]","['SUMMARY •This lecture continues negotiation looking at protocol and strategies •We discussed the monotonic concession protocol as well as the Zeuthen Strategy •We also revisited the Nash Equilibrium 9'
+ 'THE MONOTONIC CONCESSION PROTOCOL •Negotiation proceeds in rounds u where u ≥ 0 •On round u=1: •Agents simultaneously propose a deal from the negotiation set •Agreement is reached if one agent finds that the deal proposed by the other is at least as good or better than its proposal •If no agreement is reached, then negotiation proceeds to another round of simultaneous proposals 4'
+ 'THE MONOTONIC CONCESSION PROTOCOL •In round u + 1: •No agent is allowed to make a proposal that is less preferred by the other agent than the deal it proposed at time u •If neither agent makes a concession in some round u > 0, then negotiation terminates, with the conflict deal •With this protocol, negotiation is guaranteed to end after a finite number of rounds •Either the agents will reach an agreement, or a round occurs where neither agent concedes. 5'
