+What are the key components of a deductive argumentation model?,"A deductive argumentation model involves logical formulae and focuses on using logical reasoning to resolve inconsistencies. It models defeasible reasoning, which means that conclusions can be rebutted and premises and warrants can be challenged.
+
+- Key components of a deductive argumentation model:
+  - Logical formulae: Used to model reasoning and logical inference.
+  - Rebuttals and undercuts: These represent attacks between arguments, where a rebuttal causes problems for some argument extensions.
+  - Preferred and grounded extensions: Used to determine which arguments to accept by analyzing the effects of attacks.
